<h1 style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:800;">Device Analytics</h1>
<p>Understand what devices, browsers, and operating systems your audience uses.</p>

<h2>Device Types</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Desktop:</strong> Windows, macOS, Linux computers</li><li><strong>Mobile:</strong> Smartphones (iOS, Android)</li><li><strong>Tablet:</strong> iPad, Android tablets</li><li><strong>Bot:</strong> Search engine crawlers, social media bots</li></ul>

<h2>Browser Breakdown</h2>
<p>See the split between Chrome, Safari, Firefox, Edge, Samsung Internet, and others.</p>

<h2>OS Breakdown</h2>
<p>Track Windows, macOS, iOS, Android, Linux distributions.</p>

<h2>Optimization Tips</h2>
<ul><li>If 70%+ traffic is mobile, optimize landing pages for mobile-first</li><li>Use device targeting to serve different URLs (app store links, mobile-optimized pages)</li><li>Test your links in the top 3 browsers your audience uses</li></ul>
